From 2d6f8e1fe4289aed58fc80f847e4664824a312cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:48:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/52] Switch: two frames in flight, SD writes off the game
 loop, persistent pipeline cache

Console perf.log (build 6b42e83a0): the GPU needs 10-14 ms per frame but
frames took 20-31 ms because the CPU waited for the previous frame before
recording the next one; hitches of 100-350 ms came the first time something
was drawn.

- Per-frame GPU data (dynamic lights, bones, viewpoints, dynamic vertices,
  stream and matrix UBOs) is split into two regions; the command manager
  keeps a fence/semaphore bank per frame and BeginFrame only waits for the
  frame two back (DFrameBuffer::PerFrameSlot/PerFrameSlots/SyncNextFrame).
- Logs are fully buffered and a low-priority thread flushes them, rewrites
  engine-session.txt and writes queued files every two seconds; new
  pipelines no longer append to boot.log outside the GPU trace mode.
  perf.log and phase.log now live in logs/.
- The Vulkan pipeline cache is handed to that thread 3 s after the last new
  pipeline (it was only written by a clean exit, so closing with HOME made
  every session compile its pipelines again).
- perf.log counts pipeline creations and texture uploads per slow frame;
  the texture staging limit that forces a GPU idle wait is 48 MB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
